ew posts down works better I suppose, although it is honestly a bit overcom=
plicated for practical use (like, grokking that so you don't have to actual=
ly sit there and grind it out to figure out what happened is pretty painful=
). Whose idea was it for \forall to be PA KOhA and for \exists to be KOhA, =
both without any variation that doesn't need such a thing, anyway? I find i=
t leads to issues not just here but in the whole "da doesn't have referents=
" issue, since its grammar and even to some extent its idiomatic gloss make=
s it "seem" like it should have referents.
